<title>FRANCE: CAC-40 heavyweight Elf rises strongly.</title>
<headline>CAC-40 heavyweight Elf rises strongly.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in French oil company Elf Aquitaine rose strongly against the trend on Monday, helped by dollar firmness and the company's forecast of a 35 percent rise in first-half pre-exceptional income, traders said.</p>
<p>The stock, one of the heavyweights in the CAC-40 leading share index, was up 5.03 percent at 606 francs at 1052 GMT, while the CAC-40 itself was down 0.79 percent in the wake of a left-wing parliamentary election victory on Sunday.</p>
<p>The group made its first-half profit forecast last Friday.</p>
</text>
